# Keep executable scripts checked out with LF, on every platform.
#
# This is not a style preference. `scripts/telnyx/provision.mjs` begins with a shebang, and on a
# Windows checkout git rewrote it to CRLF. Vite strips the shebang when it transforms the module for
# a test, leaves the orphaned `\r` behind, and the file dies with "SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected
# token" pointing at a line inside a comment — which is what a shifted sourcemap looks like, not
# where the problem is. Node and esbuild both parse the same file happily, so nothing local catches
# it either.
#
# Verified three ways: LF alone fixes it, removing the shebang alone fixes it, and every other file
# in the tree is CRLF and fine. The shebang is what makes this file different, and the CLI needs it.
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.sh  text eol=lf
